[{"id":5332757525,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPdtsFQ","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Awesome work! I really like the refactor in `Animation::_interpolate` to call `_fetch_keys` so these cases share code.\n\nI tried this with the test project, as well as my own animations, and it solves the \"robot animation\" sort of jerk between keyframes. I'm able to take imported + optimzied glTF animations, heavily optimize them, and produce better quality results by using a modified version of \"All Tracks Modifier\" (https://godotengine.org/asset-library/asset/4332) to convert the tracks from Linear -> Makima.\n\nIn terms of why this makes sense. Linear animation has continuous value, but discontinuous derivative (velocity). Cubic animation has continous and smooth value with a continuous derivative, but theoretically does not prevent jerk. Conceptually, the extra set of keyframes should avoid jerk.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123835#pullrequestreview-5332757525","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123835","author_association":